# Line-ending policy. Deliberately narrow - there is no `* text=auto` here on
# purpose: this repo carries 519 USGS splib07 spectra plus other data files, and
# a blanket rule makes every `git add --renormalize` churn all of them.
#
# Why the file exists: with core.autocrlf=true and no rules, Windows checkouts
# get CRLF on every .sh, breaking the shebang ("bad interpreter: bash\r").
# backend/bootstrap.sh is COPY'd into the api image and runs as the bootstrap
# entrypoint, so a Windows-built image would fail to migrate or seed at all.

# Shell scripts run in Linux containers and over SSH - always LF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell 5.1 reads .ps1 as ANSI. Keep them CRLF and pure ASCII.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# USGS spectral library - byte-exact, never converted.
data/splib07_slim/** -text

# Binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.tif binary
*.npz binary
*.pt binary
